- **Suffix match:** I used `substr` rather than `like '%@domain'` so that `_` or `%` in the input can't act as wildcards.
- **Case-insensitive:** the comparison is case-insensitive, since domains are.
- **Subdomains:** `example.com` will not match `user@mail.example.com`, because the suffix includes the `@`.
